{
  "intro": "Hands-on practice in a simulated Linux terminal: organize files, answer questions from a log with pipes, write and prepare a backup script, and review how Bash and PowerShell compare. Everything is graded in your browser.",
  "labs": [
    {
      "id": "cli-files",
      "title": "Set up a project folder",
      "domain": "D2",
      "kind": "cli",
      "level": "beginner",
      "minutes": 12,
      "summary": "Create folders, copy and move files, delete a file, and find a hidden one.",
      "scenario": "<p>You are starting a new website project on <b>ubuntu01</b>. The files you need are scattered in <code>~/downloads</code>. Set things up from the terminal:</p><ul><li>Create <code>~/site/assets/images</code> in one command</li><li><b>Copy</b> <code>index.html</code> and <code>style.css</code> into <code>~/site</code> (keep the originals)</li><li><b>Move</b> <code>logo.png</code> into <code>~/site/assets/images</code> and rename it <code>header.png</code></li><li>Delete the old <code>draft-v1.html</code></li><li>A hidden file in <code>~/downloads</code> holds the staging password hint. Find it and read it</li></ul>",
      "devices": [
        {
          "platform": "linux",
          "hostname": "ubuntu01",
          "ip": "10.0.0.21",
          "name": "ubuntu01",
          "users": {},
          "files": {
            "/home/student/downloads": {
              "dir": true,
              "owner": "student"
            },
            "/home/student/downloads/index.html": {
              "content": [
                "<h1>Welcome</h1>"
              ],
              "owner": "student"
            },
            "/home/student/downloads/style.css": {
              "content": [
                "body { margin: 0; }"
              ],
              "owner": "student"
            },
            "/home/student/downloads/logo.png": {
              "content": [
                ""
              ],
              "owner": "student",
              "size": 48000
            },
            "/home/student/downloads/draft-v1.html": {
              "content": [
                "<h1>old draft</h1>"
              ],
              "owner": "student"
            },
            "/home/student/downloads/.staging-note": {
              "content": [
                "Staging hint: first pet + year"
              ],
              "owner": "student"
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "tasks": [
        {
          "text": "Create <code>~/site/assets/images</code>",
          "check": {
            "file": [
              "ubuntu01",
              "/home/student/site/assets/images"
            ],
            "type": "d"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "<code>index.html</code> and <code>style.css</code> are copied into <code>~/site</code>, and the originals are still in <code>~/downloads</code>",
          "check": {
            "all": [
              {
                "file": [
                  "ubuntu01",
                  "/home/student/site/index.html"
                ]
              },
              {
                "file": [
                  "ubuntu01",
                  "/home/student/site/style.css"
                ]
              },
              {
                "file": [
                  "ubuntu01",
                  "/home/student/downloads/index.html"
                ]
              },
              {
                "file": [
                  "ubuntu01",
                  "/home/student/downloads/style.css"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "The logo is at <code>~/site/assets/images/header.png</code> and is gone from <code>~/downloads</code>",
          "check": {
            "all": [
              {
                "file": [
                  "ubuntu01",
                  "/home/student/site/assets/images/header.png"
                ]
              },
              {
                "file": [
                  "ubuntu01",
                  "/home/student/downloads/logo.png"
                ],
                "exists": false
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "<code>draft-v1.html</code> is deleted",
          "check": {
            "file": [
              "ubuntu01",
              "/home/student/downloads/draft-v1.html"
            ],
            "exists": false
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "What does the hidden note say?",
          "check": {
            "q": "hint",
            "eq": 1
          }
        }
      ],
      "questions": [
        {
          "id": "hint",
          "prompt": "Staging hint:",
          "options": [
            "last four digits of the phone",
            "first pet + year",
            "mother's maiden name",
            "there is no hidden file"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "hints": [
        "<code>mkdir -p</code> creates every missing folder in the path.",
        "<code>cp A B DEST/</code> copies several files at once; <code>mv OLD NEW</code> moves and renames in one step.",
        "Hidden names start with a dot: <code>ls -a ~/downloads</code>, then <code>cat</code> the file."
      ],
      "solution": "<pre>mkdir -p ~/site/assets/images\ncp ~/downloads/index.html ~/downloads/style.css ~/site/\nmv ~/downloads/logo.png ~/site/assets/images/header.png\nrm ~/downloads/draft-v1.html\nls -a ~/downloads\ncat ~/downloads/.staging-note</pre>",
      "review": "<p>cp keeps the original, mv does not and also renames, mkdir -p builds a whole path, and rm is permanent. Hidden files only show with ls -a.</p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "cli-logs",
      "title": "Answer questions from a web log",
      "domain": "D3",
      "kind": "cli",
      "level": "beginner",
      "minutes": 15,
      "summary": "Use grep, cut, sort, uniq, wc and redirection to answer questions from an access log and save the results.",
      "scenario": "<p>The shop's website on <b>ubuntu01</b> had a rough morning. The access log is <code>/var/log/webapp/access.log</code>; each line is <code>IP DATE TIME METHOD PATH STATUS</code>. Answer the manager's questions and save the server errors:</p><ul><li><code>~/errors.txt</code>: every line with status <code>500</code> and nothing else</li></ul>",
