        {
          "text": "Which IP address made the most requests?",
          "check": {
            "q": "ip",
            "eq": 1
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Which path returned the most <code>500</code> errors?",
          "check": {
            "q": "path",
            "eq": 2
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Save every <code>500</code> line to <code>~/errors.txt</code>",
          "check": {
            "file": [
              "ubuntu01",
              "/home/student/errors.txt"
            ],
            "equals": "198.51.100.23 2026-11-03 09:06:31 GET /checkout 500\n203.0.113.7 2026-11-03 09:09:06 GET /checkout 500\n198.51.100.23 2026-11-03 09:11:34 GET /login 500\n203.0.113.99 2026-11-03 09:16:44 GET /checkout 500\n10.0.0.5 2026-11-03 09:19:26 GET /checkout 500\n198.51.100.23 2026-11-03 09:19:33 GET /checkout 500\n203.0.113.7 2026-11-03 09:21:54 GET /login 500\n203.0.113.7 2026-11-03 09:23:22 GET /search 500\n198.51.100.23 2026-11-03 09:29:46 GET /index.html 500"
          }
        }
      ],
      "questions": [
        {
          "id": "n404",
          "prompt": "404 responses:",
          "options": [
            "9",
            "6",
            "4",
            "15"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "ip",
          "prompt": "Busiest IP:",
          "options": [
            "192.0.2.44",
            "198.51.100.23",
            "203.0.113.7",
            "10.0.0.5"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "path",
          "prompt": "Path with most 500 errors:",
          "options": [
            "/search",
            "/cart",
            "/checkout",
            "/login"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "hints": [
        "<code>grep 404 FILE | wc -l</code> counts matching lines (or <code>grep -c</code>).",
        "The IP is field 1: <code>cut -d\" \" -f1 FILE | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head</code>.",
        "Path is field 5 and status is field 6. Try <code>grep \" 500$\" FILE | cut -d\" \" -f5 | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn</code>.",
        "<code>&gt;</code> saves output to a file."
      ],
      "solution": "<pre>cd /var/log/webapp\ngrep -c \" 404$\" access.log\ncut -d\" \" -f1 access.log | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -3\ngrep \" 500$\" access.log | cut -d\" \" -f5 | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -3\ngrep \" 500$\" access.log &gt; ~/errors.txt</pre>",
      "review": "<p>Filter, cut a field, sort, count duplicates with uniq -c, rank, and keep the top lines: that one pattern answers most questions about logs.</p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "cli-script",
      "title": "Write your first backup script",
      "domain": "D4",
      "kind": "cli",
      "level": "beginner",
      "minutes": 15,
      "summary": "Create a Bash script with a shebang, a variable and a tar command, then make it executable.",
      "scenario": "<p>You need a repeatable backup of <code>~/projects</code> on <b>ubuntu01</b>. Create <code>~/backup.sh</code> with <code>nano</code> or <code>vi</code> (or with <code>echo</code> and <code>&gt;&gt;</code>) so that it:</p><ul><li>starts with the line <code>#!/bin/bash</code></li><li>sets a variable (for example <code>DEST=...</code>) for the destination file</li><li>uses <code>tar -czf</code> to compress <code>~/projects</code> into that destination</li></ul><p>Then make the script <b>executable</b> by its owner. (This lab does not run scripts; it checks that they are written and prepared correctly.)</p>",
      "devices": [
        {
          "platform": "linux",
          "hostname": "ubuntu01",
          "ip": "10.0.0.21",
          "name": "ubuntu01",
          "users": {},
          "files": {
            "/home/student/projects": {
              "dir": true,
              "owner": "student"
            },
            "/home/student/projects/notes.txt": {
              "content": [
                "todo: ship v2"
              ],
              "owner": "student"
            },
            "/home/student/projects/website": {
              "dir": true,
              "owner": "student"
            },
            "/home/student/projects/website/index.html": {
              "content": [
                "<h1>Hello</h1>"
              ],
              "owner": "student"
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "tasks": [
        {
          "text": "<code>~/backup.sh</code> exists and its first line is <code>#!/bin/bash</code>",
          "check": {
            "file": [
              "ubuntu01",
              "/home/student/backup.sh"
            ],
            "contains": "(?<![\\s\\S])#!/bin/(ba)?sh"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "It sets a variable (a line like <code>NAME=value</code>)",
          "check": {
            "file": [
              "ubuntu01",
              "/home/student/backup.sh"
            ],
            "contains": "^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*="
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "It runs <code>tar -czf</code>",
          "check": {
            "file": [
              "ubuntu01",
              "/home/student/backup.sh"
            ],
            "contains": "tar\\s+-?[a-z]*c[a-z]*z|tar\\s+-?[a-z]*z[a-z]*c"
