      "hints": [
        "<code>nano ~/backup.sh</code> opens the editor. Type the lines, then choose Save and close.",
        "Example: <code>DEST=\"$HOME/backup.tar.gz\"</code> then <code>tar -czf \"$DEST\" ~/projects</code>.",
        "<code>chmod +x ~/backup.sh</code> adds the execute bit. Check with <code>ls -l ~/backup.sh</code>."
      ],
      "solution": "<pre>nano ~/backup.sh     # type the three lines below, then save\n#!/bin/bash\nDEST=\"$HOME/backup.tar.gz\"\ntar -czf \"$DEST\" ~/projects\nchmod +x ~/backup.sh\nls -l ~/backup.sh</pre>",
      "review": "<p>A script is a text file with a shebang, commands and an execute bit. Variables make it easy to change one value, and exit code 0 means success.</p>"
